    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/project-archivist-fixed-term/1209/100501008800": {
      "title": "Project Archivist (FIXED TERM)",
      "description": "Project Archivist (FIXED TERM) at USC We use cookies and other tracking technologies to support navigation, to improve our products and services, to support our marketing activities and to provide content from third parties.To manage your preferences, select \"Manage Settings\" or choose \"Accept\" to consent to the use of Cookies. Accept Manage Settings Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Matching job links will appear below as you type. Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to select. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Project Archivist (FIXED TERM) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180606 Category Libraries Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Project Archivist (FIXED TERM) ONE Archives – USC Libraries University of Southern California Application Procedure As part of the application, candidates must upload one document file (Word or PDF) that contains the following: 1) a cover letter, 2) Resume (including telephone and e-mail address). Closing day/time for receipt of applications is Wednesday, September 30th at 5:00pm About the Opportunity The University of Southern California (USC) Libraries seek an innovative, experienced, creative Project Archivist to join ONE Archives at the USC Libraries as the Project Archivist for a one-year contract position. The Project Archivist will process collections of archival materials from ONE Archives, one of the largest archives of lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender and queer (LGBTQ) materials. The successful candidate will bring motivation and creativity to a collegial and collaborative environment, and contribute to a safe and inclusive space. The candidate must also be knowledgeable concerning current archival theory and practice and be able to apply this understanding. Duties may include weekend and evening hours. About USC The University of Southern California is one of the world’s leading private research universities. An anchor institution in Los Angeles, USC has a large number of international students and offers extensive opportunities for internships and study abroad. With a strong tradition of integrating liberal and professional education, USC fosters a vibrant culture of public service and encourages students to cross academic as well as geographic boundaries in their pursuit of knowledge. For more information, visit www.usc.edu (opens in new window) . About USC Libraries The USC Libraries actively support the discovery, creation, and preservation of knowledge. We develop collections and services that support and encourage the academic endeavors of faculty, students, and staff; build a community of critical consumers of information; and help develop engaged world citizens. Through these means, we contribute to the continued success of the University of Southern California. The USC Libraries includes the Doheny Memorial Library and fourteen specialized libraries with an operating budget of approximately $41 million. Library collections encompass over 4.2 million volumes, 5.9 million microforms, 3.1 million images, 49,300 linear feet of manuscripts and archives, with access to over 113,800 serials in print and electronic formats, over 1,650 datasets, and nearly 1.3 million e-books. For more information, visit libraries.usc.edu. About ONE Archives ONE Archives at the USC Libraries is one of the largest repositories of lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, queer (LGBTQ) materials in the world. Founded in 1952, ONE Archives currently houses over two million archival items including periodicals, books, film, video and audio recordings, photographs, artworks, organizational records, and personal papers. ONE Archives has been a part of the USC Libraries since 2010. For more information, visit one.usc.edu Please be advised this is a one-year fixed term position. Responsibilities and Duties Reporting to the ONE Archives Librarian, the Project Archivist will: Undertake the arrangement, description, and cataloging of primary source collections in accordance with standard archival processing best practices and departmental guidelines Prioritize workloads and set appropriate deadlines; and monitor performance to ensure the timely completion of the project(s) Create finding aids for each collection, that includes writing abstracts, historical information, summary description, and inventory lists; and ensure all description complies with professional archival standards, local practice, and relevant authorities Assign, revise (or create) authorized subject headings and genre/form terms to primary source materials in accordance with national standards and local practice Undertake the preservation and maintenance of primary source collections by identifying and working with staff in implementing preventative measures for the preservation and safekeeping of archival materials; and identify endangered materials and conservation work needed Train and oversee student workers and interns Assist with the planning and promotion of project-related programs and events Work collaboratively with ONE Archives personnel and students to support public service operations and access to collections Provide evening and weekend service, as assigned Possess the physical strength and ability to lift and carry boxes weighing up to 30 pounds of materials at one time Stay up-to-date on relevant archival information trends, practices, and be able to apply this knowledge Perform other activities as needed that fall within the scope of responsibility of the position In addition, the successful candidate must demonstrate, through ideas, words and actions, a strong commitment to USC’s Unifying Values (opens in new window) . Experience and Qualifications Minimum qualifications: MLS from an ALA-accredited program or advanced degree in equivalent field One or more years of experience processing archival collections in a variety of formats Demonstrated knowledge of relevant standards and thesauri, including EAD, DACS, MARC, LCSH Demonstrated knowledge of ArchivesSpace and Excel Knowledge of current professional trends Ability to work independently as well as part of a team Flexibility and adaptability; ability to think creatively Strong research and analytical skills Excellent oral and written communication skills Excellent organizational skills, including ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines Ability of lift materials weighing up to 30 pounds Preferred qualifications: Demonstrated knowledge of establishing/applying authority control Supervisory experience Experience working in an academic library Familiarity of LGBTQ history Familiarity with basic preservation and conservation techniques The annual base salary for this position is $78,000. When determining an offer, the University of Southern California considers factors such as the scope and responsibilities of the role, the candidate’s experience, education, training, key skills, internal peer alignment , applicable laws, contractual requirements, grant funding, and market conditions. #LI-MN1 Minimum Education: \nBachelor's degree\n\nMinimum Experience: \n1 years\n\nMinimum Skills: \nConsiderable specialized knowledge of contemporary archival and records management principles and practices.\nKnowledge or background in preservation management.\nDemonstrated interpersonal, project management, analytical and research skills.\nRequires computer skills and ability to work with electronic records and databases.\n\nPreferred Education: \nMaster's degree\n\nPreferred Experience: \n3 years\n\nPreferred Skills: \nExperience as an archivist or special collections curator.\nExperience utilizing digital reproduction technologies such as scanners and digital cameras for preservation.\nTraining and experience in conducting research in primary and secondary sources.\nSupervisory ability and experience. Job ID REQ20180606 Posted Date 09/11/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Office Manager, Radio Traffic and Continuity San Francisco, California Save Job Clinical Instructor of Radiology (Practitioner) Los Angeles, California Save Job Medical Assistant (CMA) - UPC Mental Health Clinic - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Support Coordinator - Urology Clinic - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new 