    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/arcadia/patient-advocate-service-excellence-full-time-8-hours-days-non-union-exempt/1209/100767319040": {
      "title": "Patient Advocate",
      "description": "Patient Advocate - Service Excellence - Full Time 8 Hours Days (Non-Union, Exempt) at USC We use cookies and other tracking technologies to support navigation, to improve our products and services, to support our marketing activities and to provide content from third parties.To manage your preferences, select \"Manage Settings\" or choose \"Accept\" to consent to the use of Cookies. Accept Manage Settings Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Matching job links will appear below as you type. Search Jobs Keck Medicine of USC Keck Medicine of USC is a community creating a lasting impact in healthcare, and every team member contributes to a culture built on growth, collaboration, and well-being – because Together, We Are Limitless. Visit Keck Medicine of USC's Career Site for more information Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to select. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Patient Advocate - Service Excellence - Full Time 8 Hours Days (Non-Union, Exempt) Arcadia, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180702 Category Keck Medicine of USC Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) JOB ACCOUNTABILITIES • Act as a liaison between the family and care team to enhance communication, bridging gaps in understanding. Drawing on ability to empathize and look at situations from a variety of perspectives, creatively and effectively facilitates patient care services and amenities while always anticipating patient and family needs. • Acts as an advocate for the patient and communicates any gaps to the care team and assists with the resolution. • Identifies Limited English Proficient (LEP) hospital patients in the hospital each day and conduct roundings. • Identifies any patient that may require intervention in the patient care area. • Facilitates closing gaps in care by partnering with clinical care team to ensure patients receive all information needed, concerns are being addressed, and assist with the resolution as needed. • Supports clients with serious chronic or life-threatening illnesses and their families to make informed medical decisions, form effective partnerships with providers and assist patients/families in developing self-advocacy skills. Promotes an active patient voice. Facilitate techniques for patient involvement in informed decision making. • Document and process patient complaints from initial intake whether received via in writing, in person, via phone or through surveys and comment cards. Provide continuous education to staff on the patient complaint process. Make process improvement recommendation to leadership as needed. • Inputs information in the rounding log, looks for themes and global issues that can be escalated for resolution. • Orient patients to the room and hospital, including orient the use of the interpretation processes and devices. Assists the patient with basic needs including menu selection, personal needs. • Tracks and reports to the department manager/ director any issues, recognitions, and/or findings. • Communicates with staff needs of the patient/ family to nursing/ staff. • Assists with translation for on-site Educational Programs for the for LEP population. • Interprets /Translates low level communication. • Facilitates the incident reporting process to ensure events are appropriately addressed and follow-up is documented. • Alerts clinical risk management staff when egregious events are noted in the event management system or reported by the department. Assists clinical risk management staff with activities related to the identification, retrieval, and processing of events. • Performs other duties as assigned. JOB QUALIFICATIONS Minimum Education: High School or equivalent Minimum Experience: 3-5 years Experience in related field, preferably in an acute care setting Minimum Skills: Able to communicate in writing in both languages. Demonstrated interpersonal, communication and customer service skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with physicians, managers, staff, and volunteers. Preferred Experience: Experience in the medical field/ medical terminology Preferred Skills: Bilingual – Strong command of English and Chinese/Spanish language (multiple dialects preferred). Pay Transparency The hourly rate range for this position is $62,733 - $97,781 When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California Arcadia Hospital considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, State, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. JOB SUMMARY\n\nThe Patient Advocate will work as an extension of the clinical care team by identifying and resolving communication and cultural barrier using advocacy skills. This position will also be expected to manage patient expectations, including educating, and influencing expected service behaviors with staff and providers. Additionally, this position will be responsible to act as an advocate striving to empower Limited English Proficient (LEP) patients and families to take an active role in improving their patient experience while providing creative solutions to unique challenges in collaboration with leadership, the Patient Relations Representative will develop education materials, assist with policies that are patient and family centered, and make recommendation to drive service excellence. Job ID REQ20180702 Posted Date 09/17/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy Th