    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/production-manager/1209/101067476048": {
      "title": "Production Manager",
      "description": "Production Manager at USC We use cookies and other tracking technologies to support navigation, to improve our products and services, to support our marketing activities and to provide content from third parties.To manage your preferences, select \"Manage Settings\" or choose \"Accept\" to consent to the use of Cookies. Accept Manage Settings Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Matching job links will appear below as you type. Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to select. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Production Manager Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180769 Category Radio Broadcast Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Job Title: Production Manager Location: Los Angeles Classical California, a public service of the University of Southern California, seeks a technically skilled, creative and highly organized audio professional to serve as Production Manager . This position will provide essential production expertise and coordination across programming, hosts, producers and other content teams, helping Classical California deliver compelling audio experiences across its broadcast and digital platforms. About the Department: Classical California is America's largest and most listened-to public media organization for classical music. With studios in Los Angeles and San Francisco, we draw upon California's heritage of entertainment and innovation to create original musical experiences that inspire greater engagement with classical music. This is an exciting time to join as we strengthen a unified brand, expand our digital audio offerings and build capacity for the future. Position Overview: Reporting to the Executive Director of Content, the Production Manager is primarily a hands-on audio production role, combining advanced recording and editing expertise with strong project management. The position will guide multiple projects from initial concept through final delivery. The role may include concert broadcasts, interviews, hosted programs, promotional campaigns and other original audio content. Success requires someone who can move comfortably between independent editing and close collaboration, hold many details at once, work effectively with a range of creative personalities and remain calm when technical or production challenges arise. This full-time, Los Angeles-based position follows a hybrid schedule with at least two days on-site each week and additional studio presence as production needs require. Production cycles may occasionally require flexible or extended hours. Limited travel to the San Francisco station may be required for events or major projects. Key Responsibilities: Audio Content Production and Program Development – 40% Produce and edit high-quality audio content for broadcast and digital platforms while maintaining consistent editorial, technical and brand standards. Research, write and edit scripts, shaping the style, pace, format and overall sound of assigned productions. Direct and record hosts, voice talent and other contributors, including providing voice work when needed. Recording Engineering and Audio Production Operations – 20% Serve as the recording engineer for interviews, studio sessions and other productions. Troubleshoot technical challenges quickly and calmly. Select, edit and mix classical music and other audio elements, and coordinate production resources, archives, music logs and related records. Production Management and Content Initiatives – 30% Manage production workflows, schedules and resources from concept through final delivery, ensuring multiple projects remain organized and meet firm deadlines. Coordinate and supervise contributors to assigned programs and content initiatives, providing clear direction, coaching and feedback. Collaborate with programming, marketing, engineering, on-air staff and other partners to develop concepts, maintain brand alignment and ensure appropriate content clearances. Support production budgets and regulatory reporting as assigned. Digital, Fundraising and Audience Engagement – 10% Coordinate audio, social media and digital plans for multiplatform initiatives, including fundraising campaigns. Collaborate with editorial, membership and community engagement partners to support strong audience connections. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or combined experience and education as a substitute for the minimum education requirement. Five years of directly related professional and supervisory experience in audio content production, broadcasting, program production, journalism, communications or another relevant area. Advanced digital audio editing and production skills using Adobe Audition or a comparable professional platform. Demonstrated leadership, creativity and team focus, with the ability to work well under pressure and meet tight deadlines. Exceptional organization and project-management skills, including the ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining close attention to detail. Affinity for and working knowledge of classical music. Keen interest in emerging digital technologies and evolving audio platforms. Excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Seven years of relevant professional experience, including leadership in public broadcasting or content production. Professional voice work and/or on-air experience. Experience producing content across traditional and emerging formats, including web, video and multimedia. Comprehensive understanding of classical music and the interests of local audiences. Required Documents and Additional Information Resume and cover letter required (may be uploaded as one file). Please do not submit your application without these documents. The annual base salary range for this position is $90,000-$100,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Benefits To support faculty and staff well-being, USC provides benefits-eligible employees with a broad range of benefits and perks to help protect their and their dependents' health, wealth, and future. These benefits are available as part of the overall compensation and total rewards package. You can learn more about USC's comprehensive benefits here (opens in new window) . #LI-Hybrid Minimum Education: \nBachelor's degree\n\nAdditional Education Requirements\nCombined experience/education as substitute for minimum education\n\nMinimum Experience: \n5 years\n\nMinimum Skills: \nDirectly related professional and supervisory experience in broadcasting, program specialization, journalism, communications or other relevant areas. Demonstrated leadership abilities, creativity, team focus, and the ability to work well under pressure to meet tight deadlines.\nAdvanced digital editing skills.\nKeen interest in and understanding of emerging digital technologies.\nAffinity for and working knowledge of classical music.\nExcellent written and oral communication skills.\n\n\nPreferred Education: \nBachelor's degree\n\nPreferred Experience: \n7 years\n\nPreferred Skills: \nExtensive leadership experience in public broadcasting with a specialization in content production.\nComprehensive understanding of classical music and tastes of local community.\nExtensive knowledge of traditional and non-traditional production (e.g., web, video, multimedia). Job ID REQ20180769 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Provider Compensation Coordinator - USC Care MSO Finance - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Pasadena, California Save Job Account Receivable Collections, Lead - Patient Accounting - Full time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Contract Services Coordinator Los Angeles, California Save Job Production Manager Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name * Last na