    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/student-programs-advisor-ii/1209/101067476032": {
      "title": "Student Programs Advisor II",
      "description": "Student Programs Advisor II at USC We use cookies and other tracking technologies to support navigation, to improve our products and services, to support our marketing activities and to provide content from third parties.To manage your preferences, select \"Manage Settings\" or choose \"Accept\" to consent to the use of Cookies. Accept Manage Settings Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Matching job links will appear below as you type. Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to select. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Student Programs Advisor II Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180968 Category Student Support Services Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) About USC TRIO Upward Bound The University of Southern California was at the forefront in establishing federal TRiO programs on its campus. In 1977, the Upward Bound Program began and quickly grew into the Educational Opportunity Programs Center. Today, USC is proud to host six TRiO programs four Upward Bound programs, and Upward Bound Math Science Programs. The University ’ s TRiO programs are designed to help students overcome class, social and cultural barriers to higher education. These programs provide counseling, academic instruction, tutoring, assistance in applying for college admission, financial aid, encouragement and support. Academic assistance is also provided via our Saturday Academy and Summer Residential programs. The academic service provided to our students focus on English, Math, Science, and Foreign Languages. These courses are intended to enhance or complement the instruction provided at the student’s high school. Additionally, students participate in cultural, academic, social, and recreational activities. Job Summary The Upward Bound Student Programs Advisor II supports the planning, coordination, and delivery of services for program participants. The position works directly with high school students and their families to promote academic achievement, high school completion, and enrollment in postsecondary education. The advisor assists with student outreach, eligibility review, enrollment, and orientation. The position also coordinates academic and college-readiness workshops, cultural and educational activities, field trips, and other program services. Additional responsibilities include monitoring student participation and progress, maintaining program records, and supporting compliance with federal grant requirements. The Advisor II supervises instructors, tutors, and student workers assigned to the program. The position coordinates the Saturday Academy and Summer Program, including staffing, scheduling, training, program activities, student services, and daily operations. The advisor works closely with program staff to ensure that services are delivered effectively, safely, and in accordance with university policies and federal grant requirements. Primary Responsibilities Identify, recruit, and serve a caseload of eligible Upward Bound participants. Support student outreach, eligibility review, enrollment, and orientation. Provide guidance on academic preparation, career exploration, and the college-going process. Assist students with college, financial-aid, and scholarship applications. Plan and facilitate workshops, educational activities, cultural events, campus visits, and field trips. Monitor student participation, academic progress, and completion of required program services. Establish and maintain positive working relationships with students, families, school counselors, administrators, and community partners. Maintain accurate student records and enter required information into the program database. Assist with collecting data and preparing reports required by USC and the U.S. Department of Education. Help ensure compliance with federal grant requirements and university policies. Coordinate the planning and implementation of the Saturday Academy and Summer Program. Develop and maintain Saturday Academy and Summer Program schedules, including student classes, staff assignments, activities, meals, transportation, and field trips. Supervise instructors, tutors, and student workers assigned to the academic-year and summer components. Participate in the recruitment, interviewing, selection, onboarding, and training of instructors, tutors, and student workers. Ensure assigned staff complete all required hiring documents, background checks, training, and university onboarding requirements before working with students. Review instructor syllabi, lesson plans, attendance records, timesheets, and other required program documents. Provide staff with clear assignments, expectations, deadlines, and ongoing guidance. Conduct regular staff meetings and communicate program schedules, student needs, operational procedures, and assigned responsibilities. Monitor staff performance and the quality of instructional and student-support services. Address operational, staffing, student, and safety concerns and promptly communicate significant issues to the Program Director. Ensure Saturday Academy and Summer Program activities are properly staffed, organized, documented, and supervised. Perform other related duties as assigned. Reporting Structure The Student Programs Advisor II reports to the Upward Bound Program Director and works closely with other professional and student staff members. The Advisor II provides direct supervision and day-to-day guidance to assigned instructors, tutors, and student workers. Compensation and Funding This is a fixed-term, full-time, exempt, grant-funded position with an annual salary range of $68,000 - $72,413.16. The position is expected to run from October 1, 2026, through August 31, 2027, and is contingent upon the continued availability of grant funding. Preferred Skills and Abilities Strong verbal and written communication skills Excellent organizational and time-management skills Ability to manage multiple projects, activities, and deadlines Strong attention to detail and commitment to accurate record keeping Ability to work independently and collaboratively Ability to build positive relationships with students, families, school personnel, and community partners Experience planning student workshops, events, field trips, and educational activities Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, Outlook, Zoom, and database systems Knowledge of the barriers to postsecondary education experienced by low-income and potential first-generation college students Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends and travel to partner schools and program activities, as needed Preferred Education and Experience (3 years) Master ’ s degree in education, counseling, student affairs, or a related field At least three years of experience working with federal TRiO programs or similar college-access and student-support programs Experience working with high school students from low-income and potential first-generation college backgrounds Experience with student case management, program documentation, data management, and federal grant compliance Experience planning and implementing academic-year and summer programming Required Application Materials Resume Cover letter Contact information for at least three professional references Benefits USC offers a comprehensive benefits package that may include medical coverage for employees and eligible family members, retirement-plan eligibility, tuition assistance, professional-development opportunities, and access to university programs and events. Eligibility is subject to university policies and the terms of the applicable benefit plans. Minimum Education: Bachelor's degree, Combined experience/education as substitute for minimum education\nMinimum Experience: 2 years\nMinimum Field of Expertise: Student personnel administration Job ID REQ20180968 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Provider Compensation Coordinator - USC Care MSO Finance - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Pasadena, California Save Job Account Receivable Collections, Lead - Patient Accounting - Full time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Contract Services Coordinator Los Angeles, California Save Job Production Manager Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Jo