    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/associate-senior-vice-president-for-development/1209/101067475920": {
      "title": "Associate Senior Vice President for Development",
      "description": "Associate Senior Vice President for Development at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Associate Senior Vice President for Development Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20181228 Category Development and Fundraising Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Associate Senior Vice President for Development The University of Southern California seeks an accomplished advancement executive to serve as Associate Senior Vice President for Development focused on principal and transformational giving. This leader will shape and execute enterprise-wide philanthropic strategies, personally advance USC's most significant gift opportunities, and align partners across the university around ambitious institutional priorities. The Associate Senior Vice President’s leadership will encompass three principal areas: Lead a portfolio composed primarily of prospects with the capacity to make gifts of $10 million or more. Drive the closure of $25 million or more in gifts annually, including at least $10 million for health sciences and the establishment of at least one endowed chair. Provide strategic leadership for principal and transformational giving, international philanthropy, athletics principal gift fundraising, and the university’s East Coast regional strategy. The Opportunity Reporting to the Senior Vice President for Advancement, the Associate Senior Vice President will serve as both an enterprise advancement leader and one of USC's most senior frontline fundraisers. The role requires the ability to mobilize leaders and fundraising teams across a complex institution while personally advancing relationships and gift opportunities of extraordinary scale. Additional Key Responsibilities Build and advance a robust proposal pipeline, including five to seven proposals of $10 million or more, five to nine proposals in the $1 million to $9.99 million range, and at least one proposal at the $100 million level. Lead strategic planning and execution for comprehensive fundraising initiatives, aligning philanthropic opportunities across academic, research, health sciences, athletics, and broader institutional priorities. Establish fundraising priorities, governance processes, and accountability frameworks, and lead senior teams responsible for principal giving, international philanthropy, and regional fundraising. Bring renewed focus to USC's international fundraising strategy and build the organizational capacity to grow annual international philanthropy from its current level of more than $35 million toward a goal of more than $75 million. Drive the university's East Coast regional strategy and significant philanthropic opportunities supporting USC Athletics. Partner with executive and academic leaders, fundraisers, and other colleagues to advance complex gift opportunities requiring university-wide coordination and to foster a culture of collaboration and shared accountability. Support the university president, trustees, and volunteer leaders in advancing principal and transformational gift opportunities, including preparing for and staffing donor meetings and travel and participating in trustee meetings as requested. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree or combined experience and education as a substitute for the minimum  education requirement. At least 10 years of relevant professional experience, including at least eight years in a leadership role. Deep knowledge of comprehensive fundraising strategies, principal and transformational giving, planned giving, donor engagement, and advancement operations. Demonstrated ability to develop enterprise-wide initiatives, lead executive teams through complex organizational change, and build partnerships with executive leaders, academic leaders, governing bodies, fundraisers, donors, and external constituents. Exceptional judgment, communication, negotiation, and facilitation skills, with the ability to influence decisions and manage multiple high-priority initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree. Experience leading enterprise-wide fundraising within a complex institution, preferably in higher education. Demonstrated record of personally cultivating, soliciting, and closing principal gifts of $10 million or more. Experience planning or leading a comprehensive campaign and guiding organizational transformation through fundraising initiatives. Expertise in international philanthropy and global fundraising strategy. A record of partnering effectively with executive leadership, governing boards, and academic leaders on institutional fundraising priorities. The Successful Candidate The ideal candidate will have the credibility to engage USC's most senior leaders and donors, the discipline to translate ambitious goals into coordinated action, and the leadership to strengthen teams, systems, and partnerships for lasting performance. Required Documents and Additional Information Resume and cover letter required (may be uploaded as one file). Please do not submit your application without these documents. The budgeted salary for this position is $412,000 to $463,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC has excellent benefits, including health benefits for staff & their family with access to the renowned university medical network; eligibility for retirement plans with employer contributions once you meet Program's eligibility; tuition benefits for staff & their family; free professional development online courses; central Los Angeles location with easy access to commuter trains, buses & free tram pick up services; discounts to football, basketball & other campus events. #LI-Hybrid Required Education: Bachelor's degree\nPreferred Education: Master's degree\nRequired Work Experience: 10 years with 8 years in a leadership role\nRequired Skills: Knowledge of comprehensive fundraising strategies, principal giving, planned giving, and philanthropic \nengagement. Knowledge of executive leadership practices, organizational governance, and strategic planning. Knowledge of higher education advancement principles and philanthropic best practices. Knowledge of fundraising operations and donor engagement. Skill in developing enterprise-wide strategic initiatives aligned with institutional priorities. Skill in leading executive teams through organizational change and complex initiatives. Skill in building collaborative partnerships across executive leadership, academic leadership, and external constituents. Skill in evaluating organizational performance and establishing strategic priorities. Skill in negotiating and facilitating complex philanthropic strategies and partnerships.  Ability to influence executive decision-making through strategic leadership and collaboration. Ability to lead multiple institutional initiatives with competing priorities. Ability to exercise independent judgment in matters of institutional significance. Ability to communicate complex strategies with executive leadership, governing bodies, and external stakeholders. Ability to foster collaboration, accountability, and organizational alignment across multiple functions.\nPreferred Skills: Knowledge of comprehensive campaign planning within higher education. Knowledge of international philanthropy and global fundraising strategy.  Knowledge of principal and transformational giving strategy development. Experience leading enterprise-wide fundraising organizations within complex institutions.  Experience partnering with executive leadership, governing boards, and academic leadership on institutional \nfundraising initiatives. Experience leading organizational transformation through strategic fundraising and campaign initiatives. Job ID REQ20181228 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Provider Compensation Coordinator - USC Care MSO Finance - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Pasadena, California Save Job Account Receivable Collections, Lead - Patient Accounting - Full time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Contract Services Coordinator Los Angeles, California Save Job Production Manager Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from the list of options. Finally, click \"Add\" to create your job alert. Job Category Select a Job Category Academic Advising Academic Advising and Career Counseling Accounting, Finance and Banking Administration Administrative Support Athletics Auxiliary Services Biomedical Business and Financial Management Child Care Services Clinical Administration Compliance Data Analysis Dentistry Development and Fundraising Facilities Management Facilities 