    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/academic-program-coordinator-academic-operations/1209/98078822848": {
      "title": "Academic Program Coordinator, Academic Operations",
      "description": "Academic Program Coordinator, Academic Operations at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Academic Program Coordinator, Academic Operations Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20178137 Category Support Services Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Academic Program Coordinator, Academic Operations USC is a leading private research university located in Los Angeles—a global center for arts, technology, and international business. As the city’s largest private employer, responsible for more than $8 billion annually in economic activity in the region, we offer the opportunity to work in a dynamic and diverse environment, in careers that span a broad spectrum of talents and skills across a variety of academic schools and units. As a USC employee, you will enjoy excellent benefits and perks while becoming part of the Trojan Family—the faculty, staff, students, and alumni who make USC a great place to work. Opportunity to Join The USC Thornton School of Music is seeking a highly organized, detail-oriented Academic Program Coordinator to provide administrative, financial, and operational support for academic and programmatic activities . For more information about the school, please visit us at http://music.usc.edu/ . This position plays a critical role in ensuring the efficient coordination of curricular offerings, events, guest engagements, financial transactions, scheduling, and administrative operations. The position also supports the planning and coordination of recurring academic program activities and annual operational cycles to ensure the consistent delivery of program objectives in the Division of Contemporary Music . For more information about the program, please visit us at https://music.usc.edu/departments/contemporary-music/ . The successful candidate will be a proactive problem-solver with exceptional customer service skills, strong financial and administrative experience, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. This role requires sound judgment, attention to detail, and the ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. The successful candidate will demonstrate initiative and take ownership of recurring responsibilities and annual processes, ensuring projects are carried through to successful completion. The individual will serve as a proactive administrative partner by anticipating needs, monitoring critical deadlines, maintaining operational continuity, providing timely reminders and follow-up, and contributing ideas that support program growth and excellence. This position is 100% onsite at USC's University Park Campus. Primary Responsibilities - Administrative & Program Support Provide comprehensive administrative support for academic and departmental operations while working closely with the Program Chair to support the implementation of program priorities and ongoing academic operations. Coordinate meetings, events, guest visits, and special projects. Maintain and proactively manage calendars, schedules, program timelines, and recurring annual program activities. Facilitate communication among faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Manage document preparation, correspondence, and records. Support onboarding activities for faculty, guests, speakers, and other visitors. Provide reporting each semester on faculty teaching duties and assignment of students to faculty studios; monitor changes in student enrollment in specified instructional activities. Partner with the Program Chair to anticipate operational needs, monitor critical timelines, and support strategic priorities through proactive planning, communication, and follow-through. Financial & Budget Administration Handle budget tracking, processing, and reconciliation. Process purchase orders, requisitions, invoices, and reimbursements. Coordinate vendor setup and payment processing. Monitor expenditures and maintain accurate financial records. Support travel arrangements and expense reporting. Generate financial and operational reports as needed. Event & Guest Coordination Coordinate logistics for meetings, events, and special programs. Manage guest scheduling, travel arrangements, and campus visits. Support both on-site and off-site activities as required . Oversee event planning and coordinate operational resources and services, delivering day-of support to ensure events run efficiently and effectively. Data Management & Reporting Maintain accurate records, databases, program documentation, and documentation of recurring annual processes to support continuity and consistent program operations. Prepare reports and track key operational metrics. Monitor deadlines and ensure timely completion of assigned processes. Support data collection and reporting initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Two or more years of progressively responsible administrative, operations, program coordination, or financial support experience. Strong financial acumen, including budget tracking, invoice processing, and vendor management. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Excel, Google Workspace, Microsoft Office, Workday, and other technology platforms such as SIS and Concur. Strong organizational and project management skills. Exceptional customer service orientation with a demonstrated commitment to responsiveness, professionalism, discretion, relationship-building, and delivering a high level of support to faculty, students, staff, alumni, guests, and external partners. Demonstrated ability to manage projects and recurring annual processes through planning, execution, and follow-through. Demonstrated ability to work independently, prioritize competing demands, and meet deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Experience in higher education, event coordination, business operations, or administrative services is preferred but not required . Demonstrated ability to anticipate stakeholder needs, exercise sound judgment, and take proactive action to support organizational goals and leadership priorities. Additional Information This position requires regular, on-site presence and is 100% on-site at USC's University Park Campus. Scheduling flexibility is required , including occasional overtime, evening and weekend work to support events and operational needs. Due to critical business operations and peak activity periods, certain blackout periods for vacation and time-off requests may apply. Candidates do not need a music background or performance experience to be successful in this role. Demonstrated ability to identify opportunities for process improvement, operational efficiency, student engagement, and program enhancement, and to bring forward thoughtful recommendations. Why USC? USC has excellent benefits, including health benefits for staff and their family, retirement plans, tuition assistance , professional development opportunities, and access to a vibrant campus community. We pride ourselves on being a great place to work and offer: Comprehensive health, dental, and vision coverage Generous retirement benefits Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members Professional development and career growth opportunities Discounts to USC sporting events and campus activities Access to a wide range of employee wellness programs Salary Hiring Range: The hourly base salary range for this position is $28.00 – $32.50 per hour. When extending an offer of employment, USC considers factors including experience, education, skills, internal equity, applicable laws, and organizational needs. Minimum Education: Bachelor's degree, Combined experience/education as substitute for minimum education\nMinimum Experience: 2 years\nMinimum Field of Expertise: Directly related professional experience in program specialization, e.g., counseling or teaching. Job ID REQ20178137 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Provider Compensation Coordinator - USC Care MSO Finance - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Pasadena, California Save Job Account Receivable Collections, Lead - Patient Accounting - Full time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Contract Services Coordinator Los Angeles, California Save Job Production Manager Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from the list of options. Finally, click \"Add\" to create your job alert. Job Category Select a Job Category Academic Advising Academic Advising and Career Counseling Accounting, Finance and Banking Administration Administrative Support Athletics Auxiliary Services Biomedical Business and Financial Management Child Care Services Clinical Administration Compliance Data Analysis Dentistry Development and Fundraising Facilities Management Facilities Management and Construction Faculty Faculty and Teaching Faculty Development Genetics Grants