    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/digital-fabrication-technician-ii/1209/101067475616": {
      "title": "Digital Fabrication Technician II",
      "description": "Digital Fabrication Technician II at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Digital Fabrication Technician II Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20181099 Category Technician Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC)'s School of Architecture is seeking an experienced Digital Fabrication Technician II to independently oversee the day-to-day operation of the CNC fabrication lab. The technician receives project submissions, consults with students on materials and fabrication methods, prepares CNC files, and performs setup, programming, and operation of the lab’s 3-axis CNC router and multi-axis CNC milling machines. CNC equipment is operated exclusively by lab staff; students prepare project files and materials for fabrication but do not operate CNC machinery. This position is also responsible for maintaining the CNC equipment and lab, supporting fabrication needs for academic coursework and special projects, and provide support to the School’s Laser Cutting and 3D Printing Labs as needed. University of Southern California The University of Southern California is one of the world’s leading private research universities. An anchor institution in Los Angeles, USC has a large number of international students and offers extensive opportunities for internships and study abroad. With a strong tradition of integrating liberal and professional education, USC fosters a vibrant culture of public service and encourages students to cross academic as well as geographic boundaries in their pursuit of knowledge. For more information, visit www.usc.edu . RESPONSIBILITIES AND DUTIES Manage the daily operation of the CNC fabrication lab Serve as the primary operator for all CNC equipment Consult with students to review project goals, materials, fabrication methods and production schedules Evaluate Rhino models and digital files for CNC manufacturability and recommend modifications when needed Independently program, set up and operate the CNC equipment using Mastercam and Rhino Determine appropriate tooling, fixturing methods, and order of operations for student projects Coordinate fabrication schedules and prioritize projects to meet academic deadlines while managing multiple concurrent fabrication requests Perform preventative maintenance, troubleshooting and routine servicing of CNC equipment Support lab improvement projects through fabrication, assembly and installation Maintain tool library, consumable inventory, and shop documentation Assist Laser Cutting and 3D Printing operations as needed Perform other duties as assigned EXPERIENCE AND QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience Minimum of two (2) years of professional experience independently programming, setting up and operating CNC milling/routing equipment Demonstrated experience with multi-axis CNC Routers (Haas or comparable preferred) Proficient with Rhino and Mastercam, or comparable CAD/CAM software Experience translating digital design models into successful CNC fabrication workflows Ability to independently troubleshoot CNC machining, tooling, fixturing and programming issues Knowledge of materials, cutting tools and safe shop practices Strong organizational, communication, and customer service skills Other Requirements: Must possess the ability to safely perform the physical work required of all duties, including manual dexterity, agility, strength and coordination This position requires standing for extended periods, working with industrial equipment, and performing routine physical tasks associated with CNC operations Frequently: stand, walk, bend, reach above shoulder level, use keyboard/mouse, perform tasks requiring hand dexterity, hand twisting, and simple grasping; lift and carry materials weighing up to 50 lbs. unassisted; perform light to moderate pushing/pulling; move equipment and materials; and work in outdoor environments Occasionally: sit, crouch/squat, climb, power grasping, and heavy pushing/pulling Must be able to work occasional weekdays/weeknights, holidays as needed beyond regularly scheduled hours Deliver excellent student service and maintain clarity and composure when faced with difficult situations Preferred Experience: Experience working in a university fabrication lab, architecture school, design studio, or similar educational shop environment Three (3) or more years of professional CNC fabrication experience preferred, including independent project support and advanced troubleshooting Experience working directly with students, faculty and designers on fabrication projects Familiarity with laser cutting, additive manufacturing, and other digital fabrication technologies Experience supporting architectural fabrication, model making, furniture fabrication, exhibitions, or design-build projects Experience in a makerspace or physical computing environment using specialized fabrication technologies and equipment Experience with robotic fabrication systems, including KUKA robots or comparable industrial robotic platforms Application Procedure As part of the application, candidates must upload one document file (Word or PDF) that contains the following: 1) a cover letter, 2) Resume (including telephone and e-mail address). In addition, the successful candidate must also demonstrate, through ideas, words and actions, a strong commitment to USC’s Unifying Values . The hourly range for this position is $25.00-$33.25. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills,  internal peer alignment, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. #LI-AW1 Minimum Education: \nHigh School or equivalent\nSpecialized/technical training\n\nMinimum Experience: \n2 years\n\nMinimum Field of Expertise: \nKnowledge of mechanics, shop mathematics, properties of metals & plastics, & layout & machining procedures.\nMust communicate with faculty, researchers, engineers & students on mechanical matters. Job ID REQ20181099 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Provider Compensation Coordinator - USC Care MSO Finance - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Pasadena, California Save Job Account Receivable Collections, Lead - Patient Accounting - Full time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Contract Services Coordinator Los Angeles, California Save Job Production Manager Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from the list of options. Finally, click \"Add\" to create your job alert. Job Category Select a Job Category Academic Advising Academic Advising and Career Counseling Accounting, Finance and Banking Administration Administrative Support Athletics Auxil