    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/research-lab-tech-iii-supervisor/1209/101067474848": {
      "title": "Research Lab Tech III / Supervisor",
      "description": "Research Lab Tech III / Supervisor at USC We use cookies and other tracking technologies to support navigation, to improve our products and services, to support our marketing activities and to provide content from third parties.To manage your preferences, select \"Manage Settings\" or choose \"Accept\" to consent to the use of Cookies. Accept Manage Settings Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Matching job links will appear below as you type. Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to select. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Research Lab Tech III / Supervisor Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20181049 Category Laboratory Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Leonardo Morsut Lab in the Department of Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine at the Keck School of Medicine of USC is seeking a motivated and highly organized Research Lab Technician III. The laboratory develops synthetic biology approaches for engineering cell signaling, controlling cell–cell communication, and creating complex multicellular tissues. The Research Lab Technician III will support the laboratory’s research activities by planning and conducting experiments in accordance with established laboratory procedures and safety protocols. The successful candidate will work closely with the principal investigator and other laboratory members, maintain accurate research records, analyze experimental data, and assist with the daily operation of the laboratory. Key Responsibilities Plans, conducts, and evaluates research experiments under the direction of the principal investigator. Performs cell culture, molecular biology, protein analysis, microscopy, and other laboratory procedures relevant to assigned projects. Prepares samples, reagents, media, solutions, and experimental materials. Collects, analyzes, documents, and presents experimental data. Maintains complete and accurate laboratory records and research documentation. Operates, maintains, calibrates, and troubleshoots laboratory equipment. Monitors laboratory supply inventory and purchases materials as needed. Ensures compliance with laboratory safety requirements and established research protocols. Assists with the development and improvement of experimental methods and procedures. Trains and provides technical guidance to students, researchers, and other laboratory personnel. Coordinates with laboratory members and collaborators to support ongoing research projects. Performs other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in biology, molecular biology, bioengineering, biochemistry, or a related scientific field. Relevant laboratory research experience. Experience with mammalian cell culture and standard molecular and cellular biology techniques is preferred. Strong organizational, analytical, troubleshooting, and communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment. Ability to manage multiple assignments, maintain attention to detail, and meet project deadlines. The Morsut Lab offers a collaborative and multidisciplinary research environment at the intersection of synthetic biology, stem cell biology, developmental biology, and tissue engineering. This position provides an opportunity to contribute to innovative research focused on understanding and engineering multicellular systems. The hourly rate range for this position is $31.21 - $38.00. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Minimum Education: Bachelor's degree And Specialized/technical training \n\nAddtional Education Requirements Combined experience/education as substitute for minimum education \nMinimum Experience: 3 years \n\nMinimum Skills: Fully competent and proficient in the operation of sophisticated scientific equipment and independently able to perform complex procedures and techniques with accuracy. \n\nPreferred Education: Master's degree \n\nPreferred Skills: Advanced knowledge of research procedures, equipment and analysis methods. Job ID REQ20181049 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Provider Compensation Coordinator - U