    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/research-lab-technician-ii/1209/101067474832": {
      "title": "Research Lab Technician II",
      "description": "Research Lab Technician II at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Research Lab Technician II Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20181108 Category Laboratory Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The USC Department of Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine, in partnership with the Eli and Edythe Broad Center for Regenerative Medicine, is seeking a highly motivated and enthusiastic Research Lab Technician II to join our team. This position is based in the ASCEND Shared Resource Laboratory, a dynamic CIRM-funded facility dedicated to expanding access to cutting-edge stem cell technologies. ASCEND’s mission is to democratize science by making disease models, experimental techniques, and tools accessible to beginners—while also offering deep expertise in organoid culture and modeling. Job Accountabilities: Conducts research experiments in accordance with laboratory and safety protocols. Collects field and/or laboratory measurements and data. Computes results for a variety of research procedures, tests and techniques. Maintains accurate records of procedures used to conduct experiments. Uses laboratory/computer equipment to conduct analyses of experiment data. Provides routine interpretations of analyses. Handles and disposes of hazardous and non-hazardous materials in accordance with safety protocols. Maintains and organizes laboratory supplies. Monitors inventory levels and orders or secures supplies as needed. Maintains research facility in orderly, operable condition. Maintains security and safety of equipment, samples, specimens and data. Keep accurate and detailed notes and follow best TC standards and practices General Skills Excellent written and verbal communication skills and public speaking ability High computer literacy including Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Web research Comfortable with RStudio and Seurat Qualifications : Education: Undergraduate or MS degree in a life sciences field Experience: molecular biology experience, single-cell data analysis, previous teaching experience. Preferred: A strong background in molecular biology and single-cell omics Previous experience with routine molecular biology techniques such as qRT-PCR, IF, nucleic acid and protein extraction Previous experience in higher level educational topics (CRISPR, tissue engineering scRNAseq, bioinformatics, spatial transcriptomics, cell and gene therapy) Previous experience in course development The hourly rate range for this position is $25.71 - $31.30. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Minimum Education: Associate's degree, Specialized/technical training, Combined experience/education as substitute for minimum education\nMinimum Experience: 2 years\nMinimum Field of Expertise: Working knowledge of laboratory equipment and research protocols.  Knowledge of computer analysis techniques and ability to provide routine analysis and interpretation of research data. Job ID REQ20181108 P