    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/research-coordinator-ii/1209/101067474816": {
      "title": "Research Coordinator II",
      "description": "Research Coordinator II at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Research Coordinator II Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180856 Category Support Services Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Department of Population and Public Health Sciences at the Keck School of Medicine at USC has an immediate opening for a bilingual (English-Spanish) Research Coordinator II to assist in the All of Us Research Program funded by the National Institutes of Health. This position will report to the USC Principal Investigator. All of Us Research Program Goals and Summary The All of Us Research Program is funded by the National Institutes of Health and part of the Precision Medicine Initiative. It seeks to build one of the largest, most diverse biomedical data resources of its kind, with information gathered from 1 million + participants across America. This program will be one of the most diverse health databases in history. Researchers will use the data to learn how our biology, lifestyle, and environment affect health. This may one day help them find ways to treat and prevent disease. All of Us is building a diverse database that can inform thousands of studies on a variety of health conditions. Job Responsibilities include but are not limited to : Present the All of Us Research Program opportunity to eligible patients at Keck Medicine, LA General, and partnering clinics (in person or by phone). Interact with clinic staff as needed to create partnerships and increase support of the program. Help enroll interested participants by assisting with the consent process and survey completion through the All of Us research portal. Take physical measurements, vital signs and assist with biospecimen collection activities Contact potential participants to complete retention activities Use REDCap to document all patient contacts for both recruitment and retention Performs other related duties as assigned or requested. Minimum Qualifications : Bachelors Degree Willing and able to travel to off-site locations approximately once a week Strong organization, attention to detail and verbal communication Preferred Qualifications Bilingual (English and Spanish) The hourly rate range for this position is $35.53 - $38.34. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Minimum Education: \nBachelor's degree\n\nMinimum Experience: \n2 years\n\nMinimum Skills: \nAdministrative or research experience.\nKnowledge of medical environment and terminology.\nKnowledge and understanding of federal, state, and institutional research regulations as well as Good Clinical Practices (GCP) and HIPPA regulations.\nProficient with MS Office applications.\nDemonstrated effective communication and writing skills.\nAbility to multi-task.\nDemonstrated ability to work as part of a team as well as independently.\n\n\nPreferred Experience: \n3 years\n\nPreferred Skills: \nStaff education and orientation experience.\nKnowledge of Electronic Data Capture (EDC) systems and Clinical Trial Management Systems (CTMS). Job ID REQ20180856 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Rela