    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-office-coordinator/1209/99773974304": {
      "title": "Clinical Office Coordinator",
      "description": "Clinical Office Coordinator at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Office Coordinator Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20179187 Category Clinical Administration Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) USC’s Department of Neurology is now hiring a Clinical Office Coordinator to join its team. The Clinical Office Coordinator will be responsible for maintaining day-to-day clinical operational processes and systems that support the faculty and clinical leaders within the division of Headache. Crucially, this role also serves as a Patient Navigator , ensuring a seamless, supported experience for patients receiving care. We are seeking a highly communicative and detail-oriented individual who can work effectively both independently and with a multi-disciplinary team. Requirements Must be able to provide a Medical Certification. Highly communicative, detail-oriented, and capable of working well independently and as part of a collaborative clinical team. The candidate must follow established USC and departmental policies, procedures, objectives, performance improvement, attendance, safety, environmental, and infection control guidelines, including adherence to the Workplace Code of Conduct and Compliance Plan. This position is on-site and employee must report to work at the USC Health Science Campus in Los Angeles, CA when scheduled. Work hours may be subject to change depending on business needs. The hourly budgeted range for this position is $28.18 - $35.12. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Primary Responsibilities: Patient Navigation & Clinical Coordination Patient Scheduling: Schedules and coordinates all patient appointments, including seamless integration of both in-person and telemedicine visits. Referral Management: Processes referrals and acts as a dedicated patient navigator to coordinate comprehensive care across multiple internal and external specialist referrals. Order Processing: Enters, manages, and tracks clinical orders, including laboratory tests and diagnostic imaging, to ensure timely patient care. Chart Preparation: Diligently prepares patient charts for new patient visits, ensuring all necessary medical records, imaging, and intake forms are gathered and organized prior to the provider encounter. Multi-Disciplinary Collaboration: Demonstrates the ability to work effectively alongside a multi-disciplinary clinical team to ensure optimal patient outcomes. Administrative & Executive Support: Schedule Management: Provides a high level of administrative support to faculty and senior clinical leaders, including coordinating meetings with key stakeholders and making schedule changes. Often makes independent decisions regarding competing interests that must be quickly and thoughtfully prioritized. Task & Project Management: Assists with various ongoing tasks and departmental projects in a fast-paced environment. Effectively organizes daily assignments, asks questions when guidance is needed, and tracks details to ensure assigned tasks are completed accurately and on time as new needs emerge. Meeting Coordination: Schedules and coordinates various departmental and cross-functional meetings, ensuring calendar alignment and distributing materials in advance. Participates as part of a team in planning and executing department and divisional meetings. Correspondence & Communication: Creates, routes, and processes written and verbal correspondence while exercising a high degree of discretion and confidentiality. Ensures urgent and priority matters are communicated to faculty and management in a timely manner. General Office Operations: Implements systems to file, organize, and archive information. Provides general support including fielding telephone calls, receiving visitors, word processing, creating spreadsheets and presentations, processing expense reports, and maintaining electronic and hard copy filing systems. Follows established USC and department policies, procedures, objectives, performance improvement, attendance, safety, environmental, and infection control guidelines, including adherence to the workplace Code of Conduct and Compliance Plan. This position is on-site. Work hours and remote days may be subject to change depending on business needs. The hourly rate for this position is $28.18 - $ 35.12. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations Minimum Education:\nBachelor’s degree; Combined experience/education as substitute form minimum education\n\t\nMinimum Experience:\n2 years\n\nMinimum Field of Expertise:\nTwo years’ experience in an office setting. Experience with billing and compliance. Familiarity with clinical operations. Proven ability to practice discretion with confidential information. Research skills. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Job ID REQ20179187 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public tran