    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/x-ray-staff-scientist/1209/101104374352": {
      "title": "X-Ray Staff Scientist",
      "description": "X-Ray Staff Scientist at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs X-Ray Staff Scientist Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20181164 Category Research and Clinical Support Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The USC Viterbi School of Engineering seeks a Staff Scientist specializing in X-ray characterization to support collaborative research, instrumentation operations, and user training within the Core Center of Excellence in Nano Imaging (CNI), a shared instrumentation facility serving researchers across engineering and the physical and life sciences. The Staff Scientist provides scientific and technical expertise in X-ray characterization methods, including X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy, X-ray diffraction, small- and wide-angle X-ray scattering, and X-ray fluorescence spectroscopy. The position collaborates with faculty, researchers, students, and other facility users to design and conduct experiments, prepare samples, interpret results, and apply advanced characterization methods to a broad range of research questions. The position is responsible for supporting the safe, reliable, and effective operation of assigned instruments and associated sample preparation equipment. The Staff Scientist develops user protocols and training materials, qualifies independent instrument users, supports research and instrumentation proposals, and remains current on emerging X-ray characterization technologies and methods. The Core Center of Excellence in Nano Imaging (CNI) is a USC core center co-managed by the USC Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences and the USC Viterbi School of Engineering, and is co-led by James Boedicker, Co-Director and Professor of Physics and Biological Sciences, and Javakanth Ravichandran, Co-Director and Professor of Chemical Engineering and Materials Science and Electrical and Computer Engineering. Additional information about the facility is available through the USC Core Center of Excellence in Nano Imaging . CORE DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES Provide scientific and technical guidance to faculty, researchers, students, and other facility users on the selection and application of appropriate X-ray characterization methods. Train and assist users in advanced X-ray techniques, experimental design, sample preparation, instrument operation, data acquisition, analysis, and interpretation. Apply methods including X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy (XPS), X-ray Diffraction (XRD), Small-Angle X-ray Scattering (SAXS), Wide-Angle X-ray Scattering (WAXS), and X-ray Fluorescence Spectroscopy (XRF). Collaborate with USC research groups to apply advanced X-ray characterization methods to supported research projects involving hard and soft materials. Develop, document, and maintain operating procedures, experimental protocols, training materials, safety requirements, and qualification tests for licensed or independent instrument users. Conduct demonstrations and tutorials for researchers seeking to incorporate advanced X-ray spectroscopy, diffraction, scattering, fluorescence, or sample preparation methods into their work. Oversee the day-to-day operation and scientific use of assigned instrumentation and associated sample preparation equipment. Monitor instrument performance, coordinate preventive maintenance and repairs, troubleshoot technical issues, and work with vendors or service providers as needed. Establish practices that promote the safe, reliable, and efficient use of instruments, accessories, and facility resources. Work with research assistants and other facility personnel to coordinate instrument operations, user support, training, documentation, and laboratory practices. Organize and coordinate symposia, workshops, seminars, and other educational programs addressing advanced X-ray characterization methods and emerging technologies. Remain current on developments in instrumentation, experimental techniques, analytical methods, and relevant areas of materials characterization. Share relevant developments with facility users through seminars, workshops, demonstrations, and individual consultations. Contribute scientific and technical content to research proposals that require use of the facility or its instrumentation. Support or lead the preparation of proposals for new X-ray and nano-characterization instrumentation, ancillary equipment, specimen preparation tools, and other facility resources. Assist with equipment evaluations, technical specifications, justifications, implementation planning, installation, testing, and commissioning of new instrumentation. Maintain appropriate records related to instrument use, training, maintenance, protocols, and facility operations. Perform other related duties as assigned. REPORTING LINE AND ADMINISTRATIVE HOME This position reports through the Mork Family Department of Chemical Engineering and Materials Science (MFD), which serves as the administrative home for the role within the USC Viterbi School of Engineering. The position supports CNI operations and collaborates with CNI leadership, faculty, staff, and facility users across the participating schools. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS At least two years of relevant experience following completion of a doctoral degree. Advanced expertise across multiple X-ray characterization methods, including XPS, XRD, SAXS, WAXS, and XRF. Experience supporting a multi-user research facility, shared instrumentation laboratory, core facility, or university research environment. Experience developing scientific protocols, user training programs, instrument qualification tests, and laboratory operating procedures. Experience contributing to research proposals, instrumentation proposals, technical publications, presentations, workshops, or symposia. Experience evaluating, installing, commissioning, or expanding advanced scientific instrumentation. WORK MODALITY This is a full-time onsite position based at USC’s University Park Campus in Los Angeles, California. The position is not eligible for remote work and requires regular onsite presence to operate and maintain instrumentation, train and assist users, support experiments, and meet facility needs. The employee may be required to adjust the work schedule based on instrument operations, research activities, training sessions, workshops, maintenance requirements, or other operational needs. PROFESSIONAL STANDARDS Diversity, equity, and inclusion are central to the mission of the USC Viterbi School of Engineering. Viterbi staff are expected to foster a culture of support and service, model civility and respectful engagement, maintain high ethical and professional standards, and protect confidential or sensitive information encountered through their work. COMPENSATION The annual base salary range for this position is $98,836.15 to $119,497.99. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors including, but not limited to, the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s experience, education, training, and key skills; internal peer equity; applicable federal, state, and local laws; contractual requirements; grant funding; and external market and organizational considerations. Minimum Education: Doctor of Philosophy (PhD) \n\n\nMinimum Experience: 5 years \n\nMinimum Skills: Directly related education and experience in research specialization with highly advanced knowledge of equipment, procedures, analysis methods, principles, theories and concepts. Demonstrated leadership in developing new ideas and ability to publish in appropriate academic and practitioner outlets. Demonstrated independent thinking and leadership in scholarly writing according established criteria (e.g., first-authored publications, conceptual leadership in the development of publications generated alone or with others, writing of first drafts of publications and/or single-authored publications). Job ID REQ20181164 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Radiology Technologist - Arcadia Orthopaedic Surgery Clinic - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Arcadia, California Save Job RN-Perioperative Clinical Educator - Full Time 10 Hours (exempt, Non-Union) Arcadia, California Save Job Registered Nurse - 6th Floor Med/Surg Telemetry - Full Time 12 Hour Night Shift (Union) Glendale, California Save Job Instructor of Clinical Physical Therapy (Keck Hospital) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from the list of options. Finally, click \"Add\" to create your job alert. Job Category Select a Job Category Academic Advising Academic Advising and Career Counseling Accounting, Finance and Banking Administration Administrative Support Athletics Auxiliary Services Biomedical Business and Financial Management Child Care Services Clinical Administration Compliance Data Analysis Dentistry Development and Fundraising Facilities Management Facilities Management and Construction Faculty Faculty and Teaching Facu