      "title": "Perioperative Support Services Technician",
      "description": "Perioperative Support Services Technician - Surgery - Full Time 8 hours Days (7:30AM to 4:00PM) (Union, Non-Exempt) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Keck Medicine of USC Keck Medicine of USC is a community creating a lasting impact in healthcare, and every team member contributes to a culture built on growth, collaboration, and well-being – because Together, We Are Limitless. Visit Keck Medicine of USC's Career Site for more information Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Perioperative Support Services Technician - Surgery - Full Time 8 hours Days (7:30AM to 4:00PM) (Union, Non-Exempt) Arcadia, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20179947 Category Keck Medicine of USC Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) JOB QUALIFICATIONS Accountable to the Director of Surgical Services. Conducts department training for the Electronic Medical Record Scheduling System and troubleshoots problems with this system. Displays professional commitment and supports the unit team by promoting unity and teamwork among coworkers by maintaining a positive attitude and positive working relationships. Performs post-op data entry. Prioritizes appropriately and communicates information in a timely manner. Promotes positive public relations when communicating with surgeons’ offices. Responsible for understanding and participating in the organization-wide Performance Improvement Program through orientation, education, departmental and interdepartmental quality control, performance improvement, and quality planning activities. Schedules cases seeking necessary information and effectively schedules cases by Acts as a receptionist for the unit and assumes routine clerical, scheduling, and desk activities as appropriate and can work effectively in an environment that demands emotional stability, mature judgment, and flexibility. Assists with Billing duties as a relief as necessary. Assumes responsibility for computing and recording Operating Room charges on each patient. Maintains current prices on items pertaining to patient charges. Displays professional commitment and supports the unit team by promoting unity and teamwork among coworkers by maintaining a positive attitude and positive working relationships. Maintains and updates Implant log to ensure data integrity. Monitors and audits The Specialty Surgeries cases for charging and time accuracy. Responsible for understanding and participating in the organization-wide Performance Improvement Program through orientation, education, departmental and interdepartmental quality control, performance improvement, and quality planning activities. Works closely with Finance and Purchasing to ensure accurate charging practices. Works closely with Inventory Clerk in maintaining inventory on various Operating Room stock. Works closely with the Lead nurse and Nurse Navigator to ensure compliance. Assists with the Lead Nurse, Unit Nurse Supervisor and Director for assisting with daily staffing needs. Other duties as assigned. JOB QUALIFICATIONS Accountable to the Director of Surgical Services. Conducts department training for the Electronic Medical Record Scheduling System and troubleshoots problems with this system. Displays professional commitment and supports the unit team by promoting unity and teamwork among coworkers by maintaining a positive attitude and positive working relationships. Performs post-op data entry. Prioritizes appropriately and communicates information in a timely manner. Promotes positive public relations when communicating with surgeons’ offices. Responsible for understanding and participating in the organization-wide Performance Improvement Program through orientation, education, departmental and interdepartmental quality control, performance improvement, and quality planning activities. Schedules cases seeking necessary information and effectively schedules cases by Acts as a receptionist for the unit and assumes routine clerical, scheduling, and desk activities as appropriate and can work effectively in an environment that demands emotional stability, mature judgment, and flexibility. Assists with Billing duties as a relief as necessary. Assumes responsibility for computing and recording Operating Room charges on each patient. Maintains current prices on items pertaining to patient charges. Displays professional commitment and supports the unit team by promoting unity and teamwork among coworkers by maintaining a positive attitude and positive working relationships. Maintains and updates Implant log to ensure data integrity. Monitors and audits The Specialty Surgeries cases for charging and time accuracy. Responsible for understanding and participating in the organization-wide Performance Improvement Program through orientation, education, departmental and interdepartmental quality control, performance improvement, and quality planning activities. Works closely with Finance and Purchasing to ensure accurate charging practices. Works closely with Inventory Clerk in maintaining inventory on various Operating Room stock. Works closely with the Lead nurse and Nurse Navigator to ensure compliance. Assists with the Lead Nurse, Unit Nurse Supervisor and Director for assisting with daily staffing needs. Other duties as assigned. Education Minimum (Required) High School diploma or equivalent preferred Preferred (Not required) Work Experience Minimum (Required) 1-year Operating Room scheduling experience or equivalent work experience. 2 years clerical experience. Preferred (Not required) Typing skills with strong knowledge of medical terminology preferred Licenses and Certifications Minimum (Required) Preferred (Not required) Pay Transparency The hourly rate range for this position is $21.00 - $26.16. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California Arcadia Hospital considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, State, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. JOB SUMMARY\n\nThe Perioperative Support Services Technician assists with the communication between physicians, offices, and hospital personnel that is essential for the coordination of the daily activities. Following the rules established by the medical staff, schedules cases with appropriate time allocation. Applies good interpersonal and communication process utilizing verbal and non-verbal skills to achieve organizational service goals of customer satisfaction and a positive work environment. Input in computer the post-op data information. Accountable to the Business Manager. Job ID REQ20179947 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is 