    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/student-financial-services-advisor/1209/101067461488": {
      "title": "Student Financial Services Advisor",
      "description": "Student Financial Services Advisor at USC We use cookies and other tracking technologies to support navigation, to improve our products and services, to support our marketing activities and to provide content from third parties.To manage your preferences, select \"Manage Settings\" or choose \"Accept\" to consent to the use of Cookies. Accept Manage Settings Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Matching job links will appear below as you type. Search Jobs Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to select. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Student Financial Services Advisor Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20181365 Category Business and Financial Management Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The USC department of Financial Services is seeking Student Financial Services Advisors to join its team. This recruitment will be used to build a pool of qualified candidates for current openings within Student Financial Services. These opportunities are ideal for customer-focused professionals who enjoy combining financial problem-solving with meaningful service to students and families. If you are resourceful, detail-oriented, adaptable, and committed to providing exceptional customer service, we invite you to apply and join the Trojan Family. Position Overview: The Student Financial Services Advisor provides comprehensive financial guidance and support to USC students and families. This position combines direct customer interaction with detailed financial and administrative work in a fast-paced, service-oriented environment. Advisors are cross-trained to support key areas across Student Financial Services, including Student Financial Services, Student Account Services, and University Collections. This cross-functional approach provides Advisors with broad exposure to student billing, payments, account services, and collections while enabling the team to respond to evolving operational and student service needs. Success in this role requires the ability to learn quickly, exercise sound judgment, navigate complex situations, and approach sensitive financial conversations with empathy, patience, resourcefulness, and professionalism. Key Accountabilities: · Provide guidance to students, families, and campus stakeholders regarding student financial obligations, payment procedures, available options, and issues that may affect a student's ability to continue enrollment. · Review and interpret student accounts and financial documentation to accurately explain charges, credits, payments, balances, and other account activity. · Counsel students and families regarding payment options, payment plans, past-due balances, student loans, employer tuition deferments, and other available financial arrangements. · Process student account activity, including billing adjustments, deferments, invoices, refunds, payment-plan activity, account corrections, and other financial transactions. Reconcile discrepancies and ensure documentation is accurate and complete. · Investigate account issues and exercise sound judgment when resolving individual circumstances, including waiving late fees and charges when justified within established guidelines and escalating matters as appropriate. · Monitor and maintain student accounts, including updating account information, processing or adjusting payments, revising payment arrangements, lifting applicable holds, and maintaining required documentation and communications. · Provide exceptional customer service through phone, email, and in-person interactions, including sensitive or challenging conversations. Communicate complex financial information clearly while demonstrating patience, empathy, professionalism, and confidentiality. · Perform detailed back-office work, including data entry, account maintenance, spreadsheet and report review, refund processing, and other administrative activities requiring accuracy and attention to detail. · Work collaboratively and cross-functionally across Student Financial Services areas and with university partners whose processes affect student accounts, including Financial Aid and the Registrar. · Identify opportunities to improve processes, procedures, and the customer experience. Remain adaptable, resourceful, and willing to learn as systems, regulations, and business needs evolve. · Stay current with applicable policies, procedures, regulations, and emerging issues affecting student financial services and student data. Performs other related duties as assigned or requested. The university reserves the right to add or change duties at any time. Work Schedule: This is a full-time, benefits-eligible, hourly position scheduled for 37.5 hours per week, Monday through Friday, from 8:30 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Additional hours or overtime may be required based on business needs, particularly during peak registration, billing, and payment periods. Occasional weekend or Winter Recess work may also be required based on operational needs. Student Financial Services experiences peak service periods surrounding Fall and Spring registration. During assigned peak periods, employees may be required to work fully onsite for approximately two to four consecutive weeks, and vacation/PTO may not be available during those designated periods. Work Arrangement: New employees are expected to work 100% onsite during their first 90 days to support training, onboarding, and cross-training across Student Financial Services. Following the initial 90-day period, the position is eligible for a hybrid work arrangement consisting of three days onsite and two days remote per week. Remote workdays are determined by management based on operational needs and onsite coverage requirements. The primary work location is USC's University Park Campus. Employees may also be required to work at the Health Sciences Campus based on business needs. The hybrid work arrangement and onsite expectations are subject to change based on university and departmental business needs. Minimum Requirements: Bachelor’s degree. Combined experience/education as substitute for minimum education. One year of relevant experience in customer service, financial services, accounting, banking, or a related field. Ability to interpret, review, and evaluate complex financial documentation and policies accurately. Ability to counsel and advise students and parents on matters concerning financial obligations to the university. Exceptional customer service and interpersonal skills. Thorough working knowledge of all relevant state/federal regulations pertaining to student data (e.g., the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act of 1974, or FERPA). Demonstrated attention to detail. Excellent organizational and problem-solving skills, able to prioritize among several tasks. Exceptional written and oral communication skills, able to share sensitive/complex information in a confidential and straightforward manner. Extensive experience with Microsoft Office and relevant financial software. Preferred Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in finance or in related field(s). Three years of experience in customer service, financial services, accounting, banking, or a related field. Experience with relevant software, systems and platforms (e.g., Workday, Flywire, Transact Cashnet, ECSI). Experience with scanning and indexing data (e.g., DexFlow images). Familiarity with higher education environments, policies and procedures. In addition, the successful candidate must also demonstrate, through ideas, words, and actions, a strong commitment to USC’s Unifying Values (opens in new window) of integrity, excellence, community, well-being, open communication, and accountability. Employee Benefits USC offers a wide variety of benefits and programs that support our staff and their families. This support advocates work-life balance and employee well-being. USC employees are connected by the traditions and history that make us proud to be Trojans and the work culture thrives on mutual respect, trust, and synergy amongst all its members. Join us! The hourly rate range for this position is $27.32 - $30.00. When determining an offer, the University of Southern California considers factors such as the scope and responsibilities of the role, the candidate’s experience, education, training, key skills, internal peer alignment, applicable laws, contractual requirements, grant funding, and market conditions. About USC Financial Services: Financial Services consists of the following departments: Bank Reconciliation, Bursar Administration, Equipment Management, Space Management, Student Financial Services, and USCard. At USC, Financial Services, promise is to provide exceptional customer service.  We are here to help the University community! Join us – apply today! Minimum Education: Bachelor's degree \n\nAddtional Education Requirements Combined experience/education as substitute for minimum education \nMinimum Experience: 1 year \n\nMinimum Skills: Ability to interpret, review, and evaluate complex financial documentation and policies accurately. Ability to counsel and advise students and parents on matters concerning financial obligations to the university. Exceptional customer service and interpersonal skills. Thorough working knowledge of all relevant state/federal regulations pertaining to student data (e.g., the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act of 1974, or FERPA). Demonstrated attention to detail. Excellent organizational and problem-solving skills, able to prioritize among several tasks. Exceptional written and oral communication skills, able to share sensitive/complex information in a confidential and straightforward manner. Familiarity with higher education environments, policies and procedures. Extensive experience with Microsoft Office and relevant financial software. \nPreferred Education: Bachelor's degree In Finance Or in related field(s) \n\nPreferred Experience: 3 years \nPreferred Skills: Experience with relevant software, systems and platforms (e.g., Workday, Flywire, Transact Cashnet, ECSI). Experience with scanning and indexing data(e.g., DexFlow images). Job ID REQ20181365 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Radiology Technologist - Arcadia Orthopaedic Surgery Clinic - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Arcadia, California Save Job RN-Perioperative Clinical Educator - Full Time 10 Hours (exempt, Non-Union) Arcadia, California Save Job Registered Nurse - 6th Floor Med/Surg